  A: [{
    k: 'Hikoya', t: 'A Map Without Borders', s: 'Geografiya o‘qituvchisi Farruxning sinfini dunyo bo‘ylab sayohat qildirdi',
    p: [
      ['Mr Farrukh, a geography teacher, once told his students, “The world is a book. If you don’t travel, you read only one page.” He pointed to a huge map. “Each [continent] is full of wonders. This [peninsula], that [archipelago], here a deep [canyon] and there a high [plateau].” Students looked at the [volcano] on the screen and the white [glacier] next to it. “Scientists measure the [altitude] of each [summit],” he said.',
       'Geografiya o‘qituvchisi Farrux janob bir kuni o‘quvchilariga dedi: «Dunyo — kitob. Sayohat qilmasangiz, faqat bir sahifani o‘qiysiz.» U ulkan xaritaga ishora qildi. «Har bir qit’a mo‘jizalarga to‘la. Bu yarim orol, anavi arxipelag, mana bu yerda chuqur kanyon, u yerda baland yassi tog‘lik.» O‘quvchilar ekrandagi vulqon va uning yonidagi oq muzlikka qarashdi. «Olimlar har bir cho‘qqining balandligini o‘lchaydi», dedi u.'],
      ['Then he drew a line on the map. “The [equator] divides the planet into two [hemispheres|hemisphere]. Near the equator you find the green [rainforest]. In the north there is the cold [tundra], and in Africa the golden [savannah]. And in our region there is the [steppe].” Next he talked about water: the [ocean], the [coast] and the [shore], a quiet [bay] and a wide [gulf]. He showed a narrow [strait], a calm [lagoon], a river [delta] and a rich [wetland].',
       'Keyin u xaritada chiziq chizdi. «Ekvator sayyorani ikki yarim sharga bo‘ladi. Ekvator yaqinida yashil tropik o‘rmon bor. Shimolda sovuq tundra, Afrikada oltin savanna. Bizning hududimizda esa dasht bor.» Keyin u suv haqida gapirdi: okean, qirg‘oq va sohil, sokin qo‘ltiq va keng ko‘rfaz. U tor bo‘g‘oz, sokin laguna, daryo deltasi va boy botqoqlikni ko‘rsatdi.'],
      ['“Every river has its [tributaries|tributary],” he explained. “The Amu Darya’s water makes the land [fertile], but where there is no water, the land is [barren] and [arid].” He showed [vast] plains and [rugged] mountains. “The [terrain] changes [steeply], and some places remain [untouched].” Students learned that a [border] can be a river or a mountain range, and that the Pamirs are called [the roof of the world|the roof of the world]. “Some villages are almost [off the map|off the map],” he said.',
       '«Har bir daryoning irmoqlari bor, — tushuntirdi u. — Amudaryo suvi yerni unumdor qiladi, lekin suv bo‘lmagan joyda yer qurg‘oq va quruq.» U ulkan tekisliklar va notekis tog‘larni ko‘rsatdi. «Relyef keskin o‘zgaradi va ba’zi joylar tegilmagan.» O‘quvchilar chegara daryo yoki tog‘ tizmasi bo‘lishi mumkinligini va Pomir «dunyo tomi» deb atalishini bilib olishdi. «Ba’zi qishloqlar deyarli xaritadan tashqarida», dedi u.'],
      ['At the end of the lesson one student asked, “[Approximately|Approximately] how long would it take to see all this?” The teacher laughed. “A lifetime. But you can start with one step. I felt [on top of the world|on top of the world] when I first stood on a [summit].” The students left the classroom with maps in their hands and big dreams. Maybe one day they would [cross the line|cross the line] into another country and even travel to [the end of the earth|end of the earth].',
       'Dars oxirida bir o‘quvchi so‘radi: «Bularning hammasini ko‘rish taxminan qancha vaqt oladi?» O‘qituvchi kuldi: «Butun umr. Lekin bir qadamdan boshlasa bo‘ladi. Birinchi marta cho‘qqida turganimda baxtdan osmonda edim.» O‘quvchilar qo‘llarida xaritalar va katta orzular bilan sinfdan chiqdi. Balki bir kun ular boshqa mamlakatga chegarani kesib o‘tishar va hatto dunyoning chekkasigacha borishar.']
    ],
    q: [
      ['What did Mr Farrukh say about the world?', ['It is a book.', 'It is small.', 'It is flat.'], 0],
      ['What divides the planet into two hemispheres?', ['The equator', 'The coast', 'The border'], 0],
      ['What makes the land fertile?', ['The water of the Amu Darya', 'Snow', 'Wind'], 0],
      ['What are the Pamirs called?', ['The roof of the world', 'The end of the earth', 'The desert'], 0],
      ['What did the teacher say about seeing everything?', ['It takes a lifetime.', 'It takes a week.', 'It is easy.'], 0]
    ]
  }],
